{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TransferMatrix","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Trace","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.NonsingularInverse","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":28,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.transferMatrix_swap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.transferMatrix_swap","kind":"theorem","line":321,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L321-L327","doc":"Corollary: the product of any finite list of transfer matrices\nis independent of the order (for the same multiset of factors). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.transferMatrix_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.transferMatrix_comm","kind":"theorem","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L309-L319","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.signRep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.signRep","kind":"def","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L267-L289","doc":"The sign (alternating) representation of H_n(q):\nevery generator σ_i maps to `−q⁻¹ · I` (scalar matrix).\n\nThis is the 1-dimensional representation corresponding to the\npartition (1, 1, …, 1) of n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.trivRep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.trivRep","kind":"def","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L249-L265","doc":"The trivial (symmetric) representation of H_n(q):\nevery generator σ_i maps to `q · I` (scalar matrix).\n\nThis is the 1-dimensional representation corresponding to the\npartition (n) of n. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.q_inv_squared_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.q_inv_squared_eq","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L238-L245","doc":"The signed Hecke quadratic identity: `q⁻² = −HA · q⁻¹ + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.q_squared_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.q_squared_eq","kind":"theorem","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L229-L236","doc":"The Hecke quadratic identity in R_t: `q² = HA · q + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.q_from_t_mul_q_inv_from_t","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.q_from_t_mul_q_inv_from_t","kind":"theorem","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L217-L227","doc":"`q · q⁻¹ = 1` in `R_t` (using `q_from_t`/`q_inv_from_t`).\nDistinct from `QOU.Archimedean.q_mul_q_inv` (which uses the\n`q`/`q_inv` aliases in `GroundRing.lean`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.t_inv_mul_t","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.t_inv_mul_t","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L211-L215","doc":"`t⁻¹ · t = 1` in `R_t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.t_mul_t_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.t_mul_t_inv","kind":"theorem","line":205,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L205-L209","doc":"`t · t⁻¹ = 1` in `R_t = ℤ[t, t⁻¹]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.halfBorromeanConjMat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.halfBorromeanConjMat","kind":"def","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L198-L201","doc":"The conjugated half-Borromean as a matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.halfBorromeanConjWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.halfBorromeanConjWord","kind":"def","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L190-L196","doc":"The conjugated half-Borromean `h'_{ij} = σ_i⁻¹ σ_j⁻¹ σ_i σ_j`.\n\nThis is a variant of the half-Borromean where the second and\nfourth factors have flipped signs.  It represents the linking\nof non-adjacent strands in H₃(q). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.halfBorromeanMat_eq_eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.halfBorromeanMat_eq_eval","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L184-L188","doc":"The half-Borromean matrix equals evaluation of the half-Borromean word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.halfBorromeanMat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.halfBorromeanMat","kind":"def","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L179-L182","doc":"The half-Borromean element h_{ij} as a matrix in a representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.halfBorromeanWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.halfBorromeanWord","kind":"def","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L171-L177","doc":"The half-Borromean braid word `h_{ij} = σ_i⁻¹ σ_j σ_i σ_j⁻¹`.\n\nThis is the fundamental building block of the Borromean linking\nin H_n(q).  It measures the mutual linking of strands i and j\nwith all other strands as spectators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.character","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.character","kind":"def","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L165-L167","doc":"Character (trace) of a braid word in a representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.eval_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.eval_nil","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L162-L163","doc":"The empty braid word evaluates to the identity matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.eval","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.eval","kind":"def","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L154-L160","doc":"Evaluate a signed braid word in a representation.\nProducts are computed left to right: `[σ₀, σ₁⁻¹]` → `σ₀ · σ₁⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.BraidWord","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.BraidWord","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L150-L152","doc":"A signed braid word: a list of (generator_index, is_positive) pairs.\nPositive = σ_i, negative = σ_i⁻¹. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.genInv_hecke","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.genInv_hecke","kind":"theorem","line":116,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L116-L146","doc":"**Hecke relation for σ⁻¹**:\n`σ⁻¹² = −HA · σ⁻¹ + 1`.\n\n**Theorem** (was previously `HeckeRep.genInv_hecke_axiom`).\nDischarged 2026-06-08 via the docstring's suggested\n`linear_combination` approach against `hecke_rel`.\n\nProof sketch: σ⁻¹ = σ - HA·1, so\nσ⁻¹² = σ² - 2(HA·σ) + (HA·HA)·1\n      = (HA·σ + 1) - 2(HA·σ) + (HA·HA)·1     [hecke_rel]\n      = 1 - HA·σ + (HA·HA)·1\nRHS: -HA·σ⁻¹ + 1 = -HA·(σ - HA·1) + 1\n                 = -HA·σ + (HA·HA)·1 + 1\n                 = 1 - HA·σ + (HA·HA)·1\nLHS = RHS. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.genInv_mul_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.genInv_mul_gen","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L84-L90","doc":"`σ_i⁻¹ · σ_i = I`: the generator inverse is a left inverse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.gen_mul_genInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.gen_mul_genInv","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L75-L82","doc":"`σ_i · σ_i⁻¹ = I`: the generator inverse is a right inverse. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.genInv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.genInv","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L66-L73","doc":"The inverse of generator σ_i, derived from the Hecke relation:\n\n`σ_i⁻¹ = σ_i − HA · I`\n\nVerification: `σ_i · (σ_i − HA · I) = σ_i² − HA · σ_i = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.braid_far","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.braid_far","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L60-L60","doc":"Far commutativity: `σ_i σ_j = σ_j σ_i` for `|i − j| ≥ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.braid_adj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.braid_adj","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L56-L56","doc":"Adjacent braid relation: `σ_i σ_{i+1} σ_i = σ_{i+1} σ_i σ_{i+1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.hecke_rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.hecke_rel","kind":"theorem","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L54-L54","doc":"Hecke relation: `σ_i² = HA · σ_i + I` for each generator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.gen","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L52-L52","doc":"Matrix for generator σ_i. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep.mk","kind":"ctor","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L50-L50","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.HeckeRep","kind":"structure","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/HeckeRep.lean#L42-L62","doc":"A representation of the Iwahori–Hecke algebra H_n(q) of dimension d\nover the ground ring `ℤ[t, t⁻¹]`.\n\nA representation assigns a `d × d` matrix to each generator\n`σ_i` (for `i ∈ {0, …, n−2}`) satisfying:\n1. The Hecke relation: `σ_i² = HA · σ_i + I`\n2. The braid relation: `σ_i σ_{i+1} σ_i = σ_{i+1} σ_i σ_{i+1}`\n3. Far commutativity: `σ_i σ_j = σ_j σ_i` for `|i − j| ≥ 2` ","signatureChunk":0}]}